WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.670
- Hello teachers, I'm Meaghan.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.420
Welcome to Khan for Educators,

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.830
initial course for
teachers on Khan Academy.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.800
You are about to begin an
exciting learning journey.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.583
But first, let's look together
at the path that lies ahead.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.710
To get started click the
start training button

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.430
to begin learning.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.890
This course has one unit
composed of seven lessons

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.500
in which we explore everything

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.760
from getting started on Khan Academy

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.700
to classroom implementation

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.310
and diving deeper into Khan
Academy's teacher reports.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.930
The course begins with the lesson

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.830
Getting to know Khan Academy.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.700
Which shares a little about our commitment

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.040
to high quality education,
and the learning experience

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.030
we hope to provide.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.060
Then we have the lesson
Setting up you teacher account,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.380
which covers the main teacher functions,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.720
setting up classes, an overview
of Khan Academy content,

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.313
and a walkthrough of
the student experience.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.350
The third lesson, Introduction
to mastery learning

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.280
provides a broad overview
of mastery learning

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.420
and address frequently asked questions

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.590
relating to mastery learning.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.930
The fourth lesson, Using
course mastery on Khan Academy

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.600
dives deeper into Khan Academy's
mastery learning system.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.390
This lesson includes a cursory look

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.490
at Khan Academy's progress reports

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.580
and showcases teacher insights

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.963
on using progress data with students.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.540
Lesson five, Using assignments
to support mastery learning

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.900
details how to create and
manage student assignments

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.960
and how to leverage Khan
Academy's assignment report

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.333
to support mastery learning with students.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.160
Lesson six focuses on implementing

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.250
Khan Academy with students.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.950
In this lesson we go
further into the logistics

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.240
of using Khan Academy with students

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.970
including our recommended
implementation model,

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.340
classroom best practices,
and student motivation.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.550
In lesson seven, teaching
remotely with Khan Academy,

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.150
we explore implementation recommendations

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.730
and tips for teaching students

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.370
beyond the walls of your classroom.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.930
These resources are
designed to support teachers

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.570
and students in remote
learning experiences

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.673
using Khan Academy and
other educational tools.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.480
The course concludes
with a next step section

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.420
that explores the different opportunities

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.400
for further education so
you can continue to learn

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.610
and innovate in your classes.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.820
Khan for Educators was designed

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.960
so teachers, coaches, and administrators

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.290
could experience Khan Academy as students.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.620
So in order to complete the course

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.890
you'll need to engage with exercises,

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.090
master skills, and perform
well on the final assessment.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.320
But don't worry, there's
a reward for those

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.763
who complete this journey.

00:02:48.689 --> 00:02:50.630
Your professional
learning is in your hands,

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.740
start Khan for Educators
initial course right now

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.290
and find out how Khan Academy can expand

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.403
the possibilities in your classroom.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.350
Do you have any questions
about the course?

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:04.230
Access the help center
for additional support.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.063
See you soon.

